  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "What is the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061x?$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's recall some of the basic properties of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061x$:\n\n- The domain of the function is $x\\in [-1,1].$\n\n- The range of the function is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$\n\n- Its minimum value occurs at $x=-1.$\n\n- Its maximum value occurs at $x=1.$\n\n- Its zero occurs at $x=0.$\n\n- The function is strictly increasing on its entire domain.\n\nOf the given functions, the only one that has all of these properties is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13962359/assets/df22eea4331c47da3047381ca672fd80ebf75118054316fe88c0e2d96dae0d34.png)",
